{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence","id":890803,"title":"The Exigence","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Exalted","Exigents"],"posts":[{"date":"2016-05-14T14:42:13-07:00","id":890803,"title":"The Exigence","content":"I don't know if this has been covered but can the Unconquered Sun make his own Exigents from the Exigence? Or are Solars technically Exigents? Are the original Exalted still created by Autochthon or are they all from the Exigence now?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T14:45:31-07:00","id":890809,"title":"","content":"The Unconquered Sun created the Exigence as a means for lesser gods to choose their Chosen. He and the other Celestial Incarnae don't make Exigents\u2014they already have their Chosen.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T14:49:02-07:00","id":890812,"title":"","content":"There are the Exalted, as made by the five Incarna and other weird ones with less known creation mythos (Getimians, Liminals). They are Exalted.<br /> <br /> Then there are the Exalted made by the Exigence. The Exigence is a way for lesser gods to create Exalted champions. Solars are not Exigents. Solars are Exalted. Exigents are Exalted.<br /> <br /> I am not completely certain if the Original Exalted were made by Autochthon, though I'm sure he had some important role in their creation. Exigence is a completely different thing than how the originals were made.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/697-arteliex","name":"Arteliex","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar697_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"591"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T14:52:03-07:00","id":890814,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890809#post890809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unconquered Sun created the Exigence as a means for lesser gods to choose their Chosen. He and the other Celestial Incarnae don't make Exigents\u2014they already have their Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>But, why not?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T14:52:44-07:00","id":890815,"title":"","content":"&quot;What would happen if the Unconquered Sun tried to make an Exigent&quot; is exactly the sort of thing I'd expect Creations scholars to get into arguments about whilst stoned.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":11}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T14:53:10-07:00","id":890816,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890812#post890812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I am not completely certain if the Original Exalted were made by Autochthon, though I'm sure he had some important role in their creation. Exigence is a completely different thing than how the originals were made.</div> </div> </div> </div>What makes you so certain that's the case?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T14:55:23-07:00","id":890818,"title":"","content":"Alchies, presumably. Although I guess they could have their backstory changed so that instead of prototypes they're more like an application of the principles Autochthon merely <i>helped</i> the Incarnae hash out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T14:57:18-07:00","id":890823,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890814#post890814\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But, why not?</div> </div> </div> </div>A force created to empower lesser divinities to create Exalted would not be of use to greater divinities, who have already demonstrated they can create Exalted.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":12}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T15:01:09-07:00","id":890827,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890823#post890823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A force created to empower lesser divinities to create Exalted would not be of use to greater divinities, who have already demonstrated they can create Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>So, that's canon that the Incarnae were the sole creators of their exalted?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T15:08:29-07:00","id":890829,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890827#post890827\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> So, that's canon that the Incarnae were the sole creators of their exalted?</div> </div> </div> </div>That's not a statement I intended to make. I'm avoiding specifics about Autocthon because I don't know any canonically specific information about him in Ex3.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T15:20:26-07:00","id":890836,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890829#post890829\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That's not a statement I intended to make. I'm avoiding specifics about Autocthon because I don't know any canonically specific information about him in Ex3.</div> </div> </div> </div>So you don't know. Okay, that's fine. Maybe it will get answered in time, maybe not.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T15:49:44-07:00","id":890846,"title":"","content":"Auto who?<br /> <br /> 10chars","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T15:53:17-07:00","id":890847,"title":"","content":"The Exigence is there to show that Exaltation is myriad in its forms and origins. Plugging everything into the Exigence is rather missing the point.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/75951-ex3-why-gods-need-the-exigence\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Why Gods Need the Exigence</a> - Plot hooks for Exigent characters of various gods.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/113648-ex3-homebrew-solar-charms\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] Homebrew Solar Charms</a> - I can see the future, and it is glorious.<br /> <a href=\"https://glasslibrary.wordpress.com/\" target=\"_blank\">[Ex3] The Glass Library</a> - My Exalted Third Edition Blog (Updated 24/04/2016)","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/54-tiresias","name":"Tiresias","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar54_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2340"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T16:32:41-07:00","id":890857,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890846#post890846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auto who?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a kind of curdled Serbian cheese made with the milk of alpine marmots. Complex and interesting at first, but with a bitter aftertaste.<br /> <br /> I don't know what it has to do with anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":2093,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","user":"Crumplepunch","date":". 05-14-2016, 07:36 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T17:07:54-07:00","id":890870,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890846#post890846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auto who?<br /> <br /> 10chars</div> </div> </div> </div>One of the Primordials, named Autochthon, The Great Maker, assisted the Gods in their rebellion. He played an important part in the Exaltation process, though what, specifically, that part was is unclear. After the Primordial War, he left.<br /> <br /> For more information on what happened after that, I suggest looking at the 2e Compass of Celestial Directions - Autochthonia.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>....","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/226-brilliantrain","name":"BrilliantRain","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar226_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3718"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T18:20:57-07:00","id":890894,"title":"","content":"I like Games of Divinity's take on Autochthon - he was a trickster as much as a tinker, who told the gods secrets that helped them make that which might slay their enemies. Note that it didn't say &quot;he made a bunch of 'blank' Exaltations, then the Incarnae flavored them with their respective secret sauces.&quot; That's an important distinction. Then he taught the Exalted secrets in working the Magical Materials.<br /> <br /> If Autochthon's gonna feature in Ex3, that's all the role he needs in their creation myth.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890809#post890809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unconquered Sun created the Exigence as a means for lesser gods to choose their Chosen. He and the other Celestial Incarnae don't make Exigents\u2014they already have their Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Plus they're not &quot;lesser gods.&quot; <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890823#post890823\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">A force created to empower lesser divinities to create Exalted would not be of use to greater divinities, who have already demonstrated they can create Exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, wait, I guess you said that before me. Dammit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Arteliex</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890812#post890812\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">There are the Exalted, as made by the five Incarna\u2026</div> </div> </div> </div>Incarna is singular - Incarnae is plural. More important, there are seven of them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-14-2016, 10:33 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T19:55:07-07:00","id":890934,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890846#post890846\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Auto who?</div> </div> </div> </div>...you're on the internet. Maybe try a search for &quot;Autochton Exalted&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T20:33:07-07:00","id":890949,"title":"","content":"Pretty sure he was kidding. Possibly as some kind of dig at the excessive prominence of Auto in late 2e fandom descriptions of Exaltation.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-14T20:44:20-07:00","id":890954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890949#post890949\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Pretty sure he was kidding. Possibly as some kind of dig at the excessive prominence of Auto in late 2e fandom descriptions of Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>Late, nothing. Heck, &quot;Exaltation,&quot; nothing.<br /> <br /> I remember so clearly coming into the Exalted fandom (after a brief and disastrous flirtation with 1E Lunars) with the 2E core, going online and... suddenly every conversation is about a robot dragon from outer space. No such entity had been mentioned in the Corebook, so I was <i>really</i> unprepared for it to be central to every part of the setting.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T03:23:19-07:00","id":891065,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890954#post890954\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Late, nothing. Heck, &quot;Exaltation,&quot; nothing.<br /> <br /> I remember so clearly coming into the Exalted fandom (after a brief and disastrous flirtation with 1E Lunars) with the 2E core, going online and... suddenly every conversation is about a robot dragon from outer space. No such entity had been mentioned in the Corebook, so I was <i>really</i> unprepared for it to be central to every part of the setting.</div> </div> </div> </div>Exalted: The Autochthonians was the last major release of 1e, and included the Locust Crusade, which was effectively the 1e version of Return of the Scarlet Empress. Although a lot of it was later discarded, it still laid the groundwork for all the cruft that would later build up around Autochthon and his works throughout 2e.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T06:22:01-07:00","id":891112,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Robert Vance</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=890809#post890809\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Unconquered Sun created the Exigence as a means for lesser gods to choose their Chosen. He and the other Celestial Incarnae don't make Exigents\u2014they already have their Chosen.</div> </div> </div> </div>Now that I think about it, could the Unconquered Sun's Exigence be used for a purpose other than providing lesser gods with means to create their own chosen?<br /> <br /> For example say some sorceror managed to get access to Exigence from a minor god he has dealings with, who in turn got it from the Unconquered Sun. What might he be able to do with it?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6615-swazzle","name":"Swazzle","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"16"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T06:59:00-07:00","id":891126,"title":"","content":"Exalted being Exalted, you might not be surprised if Luna looked at the Exigence, saw that occasionally Exalted as mighty as the Solars themselves were born from it and thought &quot;Hmmm. Perhaps some Moon chosen, strengthened by the power of the sun, would be a good thing? I should talk to the Unconquered Sun about this, as a collaborative project. After all, we have the same goals in mind, broadly.&quot;. <br /> <br /> At the same time, it is of course very easy for the setting to simply technobabble that &quot;Different Celestial Essences are not compatible to forge Exaltation&quot; or something like that and have that just be true.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/929-ghosthead","name":"Ghosthead","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2113"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T07:06:42-07:00","id":891128,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Swazzle</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891112#post891112\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Now that I think about it, could the Unconquered Sun's Exigence be used for a purpose other than providing lesser gods with means to create their own chosen?<br /> <br /> For example say some sorceror managed to get access to Exigence from a minor god he has dealings with, who in turn got it from the Unconquered Sun. What might he be able to do with it?</div> </div> </div> </div>A very interesting line of thought, but probably one that will be left for Storytellers to decide.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Developer for Exalted<br /> <br /> Want to write for Exalted? Look at the <a href=\"http://theonyxpath.com/submission-guidelines/\" target=\"_blank\">freelancer submission guidelines.</a><br /> <br /> <a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/user?u=451515\" target=\"_blank\">Robert Vance's Patreon</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/527-robert-vance","name":"Robert Vance","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar527_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10044"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T07:39:40-07:00","id":891146,"title":"","content":"This is an interesting thread. Because it opens up the question of whether the Incarnae might create specialized shock troops. I.E. the Unconquered Sun doesn't need another Solar, but would like someone for a specific task that he has in mind. So he might whip up an exigent for that specific task as a one off. Could make for some interesting plots.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4498-ardis","name":"Ardis","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"32"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T10:47:33-07:00","id":891240,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence#post890803\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't know if this has been covered but can the Unconquered Sun make his own Exigents from the Exigence? Or are Solars technically Exigents? Are the original Exalted still created by Autochthon or are they all from the Exigence now?</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> In my &quot;fluff&quot; (and there is no difinitive Answer until the book on Exigents is released) - the Exigents are an Exalted with qualitied of the God that exalted them. As such I'd say the Solar Exalted can be considered Sun Exigents, the Lunar Exalted are Moon Exigents, the Sidereal are Star Exigents (etc...).<br /> <br /> So my answer is you and no - the Solars are Exigents, and thus the Sun cannot make his own because he already has. And if he were to do so, he'd essentially be making the Solar Souls increase beyond 300.<br /> <br /> The Logic I have behind this is that the Sun made 300 souls, Lunar made 300, but each Star Maiden made only 60 (60 x 5 = 300). Exigence is a MASSIVELY draining process that can be fatal to lesser gods - and I consider the UCS and Lunar to be two of the most powerful of the Gods, and the Maidens the only ones to come second to them since these 7 are almost always present regardless of where in Creation you are. Thus the most powerful could only manage 300 and were probably near death once done.<br /> <br /> The Exigents are the chosen of lesser Gods - probably capable of making only a few souls. I suspect VERY few would be capable of even making more than 10.<br /> <br /> In the end however, your game is your game. If you feel the Sun can make a new type of Exalted - go for it! Its all RPG story creating and, if your idea is cool, go for it :P","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Support new ideas. If you must criticize, always offer advice to the creator on how they could improve, or even suggest alternative solutions to fix a problem you can see. Dismissive comments should be equally dismissed as attempts to grab attention. Focus only on contributions that help you grow and develop, and ignore jealous efforts to stunt your creative sparks.</i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5915-zenvious","name":"zenvious","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"152"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:04:14-07:00","id":891255,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>zenvious</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891240#post891240\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In my &quot;fluff&quot; the Exigents are an Exalted with qualities of the God that exalted them.</div> </div> </div> </div>There's already a word for that: &quot;Exalted&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:11:11-07:00","id":891261,"title":"","content":"The Solars aren't Exigents because Exigents are Exalts made using the Exigence, which the Sun (indeed, all the Incarnae) didn't need to use to make his Exalts.<br /> <br /> Neither, for that matter, is a square a triangle.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-15-2016, 02:18 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:14:17-07:00","id":891264,"title":"","content":"Exigent is not really a nomenclature the way it's being used here. They're Exalted. &quot;Exigent&quot; refers more to the bureaucratic policy that defined how they came into existence. So, there is no &quot;Solar Exigent.&quot; <br /> <br /> To answer the OP: The Incarnae can't make any more Exalts, with or without the Exigence. (And they didn't need the Exigence in the first place.)","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":14}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke","name":"John M\u00f8rke","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar86_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"416"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:15:03-07:00","id":891266,"title":"","content":"I think there's basically two definitions of &quot;Exigent&quot; that fortunately line up quite neatly. To the gods and savants, an exigent is an exalted created by a Sun-assisted process by gods who would not otherwise be capable of it.<br /> <br /> To the general populace of creation, an Exigent is an exalted which is neither Anathema or Dragon-Blooded, whose powers are miscellaneous and varied to the point of defying any rigid classification.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:22:50-07:00","id":891271,"title":"","content":"The player community is naturally going to trend toward discussing &quot;Exigents&quot; as a category but that's not really how they work in the setting or how they're thought of. Outside of a few very technical First Age treatises, you won't really see anyone considering unique Exalts as belonging to a big group-category of &quot;Exigents.&quot; Just about everyone in Creation-- including elder Lunars and Sidereals-- would look at Strawmaiden Janest as &quot;the Harvest Exalt&quot; &quot;the Chosen of Ten Sheaves&quot; rather than &quot;an Exigent of a field god.&quot; The latter implies a commonality with, say, Thousand Venoms Mistress, which, holy damn, no, those two have less in common than a Solar and a Lunar do.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":21}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden","name":"Holden","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar84_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"673"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T11:41:22-07:00","id":891283,"title":"","content":"Makes sense. It's not like Farmer Joe knows there's a fountain full of divine fire in the Jade Pleasure Dome or wherever it is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T13:13:58-07:00","id":891335,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891271#post891271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The player community is naturally going to trend toward discussing &quot;Exigents&quot; as a category but that's not really how they work in the setting or how they're thought of. Outside of a few very technical First Age treatises, you won't really see anyone considering unique Exalts as belonging to a big group-category of &quot;Exigents.&quot; Just about everyone in Creation-- including elder Lunars and Sidereals-- would look at Strawmaiden Janest as &quot;the Harvest Exalt&quot; &quot;the Chosen of Ten Sheaves&quot; rather than &quot;an Exigent of a field god.&quot; The latter implies a commonality with, say, Thousand Venoms Mistress, which, holy damn, no, those two have less in common than a Solar and a Lunar do.</div> </div> </div> </div>This leaves me with both a sigh and a meh. I miss the days when I felt that the original 4 (or 5) Creation Exalted felt like they were unique in a world filled with supernatural creatures. Now that the UCS is Oprah-ing exaltations out to everyone I just find this new world boring. Weren't we happy with God-blooded?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T13:41:02-07:00","id":891344,"title":"","content":"Oh, sure, when you put it in puerile terms like &quot;Oprah-ing Exaltations out to everybody,&quot; it's gonna sound shitty. But anything can be made to sound awful.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891335#post891335\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Weren't we happy with God-blooded?</div> </div> </div> </div>Nope.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T13:44:29-07:00","id":891346,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891344#post891344\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Nope.</div> </div> </div> </div>&quot;<i> Strawmaiden Janest as &quot;the Harvest Exalt&quot;' sounds like possibly the lamest thing I've ever heard. </i><br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T13:50:35-07:00","id":891349,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891346#post891346\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> &quot;<i> Strawmaiden Janest as &quot;the Harvest Exalt&quot;' sounds like possibly the lamest thing I've ever heard. </i></div> </div> </div> </div>Would you say that if she had her grimscythe hooked around your neck and was about to harvest your life?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/188-yeoflittlefaith","name":"YeOfLittleFaith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar188_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1159"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T13:52:56-07:00","id":891350,"title":"","content":"Not to mention it's a pretty gross exaggeration to say he's giving them out to &quot;everyone&quot; when it's pretty explicitly stated as a rare and special thing for a god to be granted the Exigence. If there are 200 more people with superpowers in the world, does that really make the world that much smaller? Even if it was 400? 1000? You could exalt an entire (large) high school and it would more than cover the number of exalts in the world not counting the dragon blooded. And frankly, adding them is basically just exalting like 6-10 more high schools. <br /> <br /> That would hardly be noticeable in the scope of the world. A world that is bigger and more spread out than ours. If you don't care for the Exigence, that's cool. I find flaws in the arguments you've presented, but it doesn't make your base opinion invalid for you. That said, I get the impression that your thoughts on Strawmaiden Janest come from not having read the story fiction in the core book introducing her, which really helps sell it in my opinion.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>I post Artifacts in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/823884-3e-the-artifact-and-evocation-workshop\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>. How I make them is in <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/828820-how-to-write-artifacts-and-evocations\" target=\"_blank\">this thread</a>.<br /> I have made many tools and other things for 3rd Edition. I now host all of my creations on my Google site: <a href=\"https://sites.google.com/site/unsungherovault/home\" target=\"_blank\">The Vault of the Unsung Hero</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/368-the-unsung-hero","name":"The Unsung Hero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar368_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2288"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T14:01:42-07:00","id":891356,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891350#post891350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Not to mention it's a pretty gross exaggeration to say he's giving them out to &quot;everyone&quot; when it's pretty explicitly stated as a rare and special thing for a god to be granted the Exigence. If there are 200 more people with superpowers in the world, does that really make the world that much smaller? Even if it was 400? 1000? You could exalt an entire (large) high school and it would more than cover the number of exalts in the world not counting the dragon blooded. And frankly, adding them is basically just exalting like 6-10 more high schools.</div> </div> </div> </div>Quality over quantity, I'd say. It's more about the fact that an exalt can come from a river god or a trash god instead of something as mighty as the Incarnae bothers me. This is where God-blooded, pleasantly, fit in. Spirit charms fit in nicely too. Having them go through apotheosis at Essence 3 was a nice touch. Calling them Exalts is lame. <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Unsung Hero</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891350#post891350\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That would hardly be noticeable in the scope of the world. A world that is bigger and more spread out than ours. If you don't care for the Exigence, that's cool. I find flaws in the arguments you've presented, but it doesn't make your base opinion invalid for you. That said, I get the impression that your thoughts on Strawmaiden Janest come from not having read the story fiction in the core book introducing her, which really helps sell it in my opinion.</div> </div> </div> </div>I've read the entire core. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T14:06:26-07:00","id":891362,"title":"","content":"But, I digress. My feelings on Exigents doesn't really answer my questions.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T14:30:32-07:00","id":891373,"title":"","content":"Hmmmm.. in that case, may I dig up a (probably old by now) suggestions that either Exigents are now god-blooded &amp; scrap the Exaltations notion, or get rid of god-blooded &amp; only have Exigents? I don't get the thematic point of having both.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://wondrousatlas.wordpress.com\" target=\"_blank\">Wondrous Atlas of Creation's Destiny</a> - I cohost an Exalted podcast focusing on examining the setting's lore and how to develop them into elements to use in games.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/924488-homebuilt-exalted-st-screen-reference-sheet\" target=\"_blank\">Ex3 Reference Materials</a> - currently includes an ST screen, common actions sheet, weapons reference sheet, character creation summary and mortal QCs reference sheet.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/497-xerxes","name":"Xerxes","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar497_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"557"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T14:42:25-07:00","id":891379,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891373#post891373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> I don't get the thematic point of having both.</div> </div> </div> </div>I get the &quot;YAY NEW!!!&quot; buzz of the new exalts but on reflection this is my feelings as well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:02:29-07:00","id":891390,"title":"","content":"The same reason we have elemental-blooded and terrestrial exalted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:16:07-07:00","id":891400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891390#post891390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The same reason we have elemental-blooded and terrestrial exalted.</div> </div> </div> </div>That's just a cute word for God-blooded. Terrestrials fit a very specific niche in the world, one that I don't think exigents do. Apples and Oranges","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:18:29-07:00","id":891403,"title":"","content":"I think your questions were pretty well answered already. The Sun can't make Exigents, Solars aren't Exigents, and Autochthon is being de-emphasized but I wouldn't bet on him being entirely uninvolved.<br /> <br /> I don't think godbloods and Exigents are redundant. Actually, I don't even think they're very similar. Godbloods are literally people with the blood of gods. They've got gods as family. They might get a bit of magic but they're not Exalted.<br /> <br /> Exigents are gonna be a lot more powerful, with a completely different relationship to their patrons.<br /> <br /> PS: Would you like the new splats better if they didn't use the E-word for them?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:22:15-07:00","id":891406,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891403#post891403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think your questions were pretty well answered already. The Sun can't make Exigents, Solars aren't Exigents, and Autochthon is being de-emphasized but I wouldn't bet on him being entirely uninvolved.</div> </div> </div> </div>These were guesses at best. *Edit: Sorry, I didn't see John's response.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891403#post891403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think godbloods and Exigents are redundant. Actually, I don't even think they're very similar. Godbloods are literally people with the blood of gods. They've got gods as family. They might get a bit of magic but they're not Exalted.<br /> <br /> Exigents are gonna be a lot more powerful, with a completely different relationship to their patrons.</div> </div> </div> </div>Meh.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Sanctaphrax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891403#post891403\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">PS: Would you like the new splats better if they didn't use the E-word for them?</div> </div> </div> </div>I've already stated a yes to this.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3230,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","user":"Tyzerg","date":". 05-15-2016, 06:47 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:23:21-07:00","id":891407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Xerxes</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891373#post891373\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hmmmm.. in that case, may I dig up a (probably old by now) suggestions that either Exigents are now god-blooded &amp; scrap the Exaltations notion, or get rid of god-blooded &amp; only have Exigents? I don't get the thematic point of having both.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thematically?<br /> Exigence is a dangerous way to get a powerful champion probably as a last ditch effort.<br /> God Blooded are more often than not the spirit's actual kids. Permanent essence endowment is really rare and arguably dilutes them.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":7,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","user":"Lioness","date":". 05-15-2016, 06:30 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:35:58-07:00","id":891412,"title":"","content":"Do we even still need endowment-created god blooded any more?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:38:43-07:00","id":891414,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891412#post891412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we even still need endowment-created god blooded any more?</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably not, although that would be cool for Gods who can't do the whole exigence thing or for whatever reason can't have god-blooded the more &quot;natural&quot; way. Or maybe as like a test run for a possible exigent. Or like you could have god-blooded &quot;super saiyan&quot; into exigents. That might be neat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:42:51-07:00","id":891416,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891412#post891412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we even still need endowment-created god blooded any more?</div> </div> </div> </div>To be fair, with God-Blooded no longer having enlightened Essence and spirit Charms as the default*, and probably not having a rote set of mechanics, there's not much difference between being the son of a sea-god (and maybe being able to breathe water or talk to dolphins) and having the favor of a sea-god (and maybe being able to breathe water or talk to dolphins).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891414#post891414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or like you could have god-blooded &quot;super saiyan&quot; into exigents. That might be neat.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, thanks, I'll pass. Part of the risk of seeking the Exigence is the diminishment that comes with it; a god's blessing randomly mutating into an Exaltation both carries none of that risk <i>and</i> manages to cheapen Exaltation far more than Exigence itself.<br /> <br /> Hey, remember when Goku went Super Saiyan as the culmination of an entire saga's buildup, where Freeza killed off an entire planet over the <i>possibility</i> of it, where Vegeta spoke of legends in which it happened only every thousand years, and its occurrence left King Kai in awe? Then do you remember where Trunks, Vegeta, and Gohan all achieved it without <i>any</i> of that buildup? Shit, <i>Trunks' introduction to the series</i> had him going Super Saiyan, as if to show the viewers how dumb they were for buying into the hype.<br /> <br /> *<i>If</i> they have enlightened Essence and Charms, it'll be their own Charms, don't forget that!","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-15-2016, 07:16 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:47:31-07:00","id":891418,"title":"","content":"Good point.<br /> <br /> All in all I suspect there will be sufficient differentiation between exigent and god blooded once we have rules for both that it will be obvious that they fill very different thematic niches.<br /> <br /> *Looks at writers* <i>Right guys? </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T15:50:09-07:00","id":891421,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891264#post891264\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Exigent is not really a nomenclature the way it's being used here. They're Exalted. &quot;Exigent&quot; refers more to the bureaucratic policy that defined how they came into existence. So, there is no &quot;Solar Exigent.&quot;<br /> <br /> To answer the OP: The Incarnae can't make any more Exalts, with or without the Exigence. (And they didn't need the Exigence in the first place.)</div> </div> </div> </div>Fair enough. Although what separates the Incarnae exalted and all the others is basically just &quot;because we said they are different.&quot; Please, work on making that better.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T16:14:52-07:00","id":891429,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891421#post891421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although what separates the Incarnae exalted and all the others is basically just &quot;because we said they are different.&quot; Please, work on making that better.</div> </div> </div> </div>What separates [insert complex and obscure thing] from [insert complex and obscure, but superficially similar thing]? Aside from someone knowledgeable telling laymen that they're different and how they're different, like John M\u00f8rke's been doing <b>for years</b>?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":177,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","user":"TheCountAlucard","date":". 05-16-2016, 11:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T16:25:29-07:00","id":891433,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891412#post891412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we even still need endowment-created god blooded any more?</div> </div> </div> </div>No, we don't. Endowment took a permanent willpower out of the God, which was a permanent diminishment - some people assumed they would just recoup that with their passive XP gain, but that was never even the goal of 2e (which, you know, specifically states that NPCs do not use XP). It is a major, major sacrifice in their part, and meant to be as ridiculously rare... as the Exigence. It was not treated as THAT rare, in-play, because the benefits were minor enough that people wanted many of them. But that's the thing - it was always the spirit losing a part of himself to empower someone, who then... got pretty much no powers, just the potential to develop some, with difficulty. An Exalted fits MUCH better with how they were actually used in-play: Spirit spends stuff, gains a powerful champion.<br /> <br /> As Alucard says, Divine Favor is something we will still have, but in potency and style, it's very different from 'I made you an ess-using powerhouse flavored by me.'<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T16:42:52-07:00","id":891443,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891421#post891421\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Although what separates the Incarnae exalted and all the others is basically just &quot;because we said they are different.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>Probably don't have a culture hero who shuffles power and identity around with masks. Probably don't have the Chosen of a minor god as the kind of hero real life people attribute civilisation to.<br /> <br /> The Exalted we've had before reference the iconic. The new Exalted, particularly Exigents, seem more focused in the novel and obscure.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">&quot;<i>Strawmaiden Janest as &quot;the Harvest Exalt&quot; sounds like possibly the lamest thing I've ever heard.</i></div> </div> </div> </div> Yes, nobody ever attached dramatic connotations to the word &quot;har-https://s-media-cache-ak0.pinimg.com/736x/58/99/4c/58994cc8adec19e4b6abd9cbe351f1b9.jpg<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":158,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","user":"Isator Levi","date":". 05-15-2016, 08:01 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T16:49:34-07:00","id":891444,"title":"","content":"I think a distinction between an Exalt and an endowed/adopted God-Blood could be apparent if Exalted aren't just considered a package of generic superpowers, devoid of context or purpose.<br /> <br /> Like designing Exigents, I suppose some of this might be helped by focusing on a god specifically, rather than gods abstractly and generically; to think of the circumstances in which Ten Sheaves might breathe a bit of power into somebody to make them a bit more like him or express qualities of his lineage, versus the chosen divine champion raised to glory that she might scythe down the hordes of chaos that would devour the land he loved.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T17:27:17-07:00","id":891462,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891429#post891429\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What separates [insert complex and obscure thing] from [insert complex and obscure, but superficially similar thing]? Aside from someone telling folks they're different and how they're different like John M\u00f8rke's been doing <b>for years</b>?</div> </div> </div> </div>I await the answer with bated breath.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T17:33:35-07:00","id":891468,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891443#post891443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Probably don't have a culture hero who shuffles power and identity around with masks. Probably don't have the Chosen of a minor god as the kind of hero real life people attribute civilisation to.<br /> <br /> The Exalted we've had before reference the iconic. The new Exalted, particularly Exigents, seem more focused in the novel and obscure.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>Yeah, I wouldn't associate Sidereals with novel or obsure at all *eye roll* And I'm not playing Exalted for the minor characters. I'm playing Exalted for the Champions of Awesome. Exigents are NPCs at best. Be cool anathema for Dragon-blooded to slay. <br /> <br /> Anyways, that's not what I was saying. I was saying that it is pretty lame that the celestials and terrestrials were made by &quot;insert magic here&quot; and the exigents are created through the exigence. At least with Autochthon we had an answer (one of the creators of reality did it). This doesn't feel in theme for any of the Incarnae and the Exigence doesn't feel in theme for the Sun at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T17:44:34-07:00","id":891475,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891416#post891416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">To be fair, with God-Blooded no longer having enlightened Essence and spirit Charms as the default*, and probably not having a rote set of mechanics, there's not much difference between being the son of a sea-god (and maybe being able to breathe water or talk to dolphins) and having the favor of a sea-god (and maybe being able to breathe water or talk to dolphins).</div> </div> </div> </div> Ah, the old Holden 3rd edition special. It was TEDIOUS to read through everyone's individual charms in the Antagonist section. If every demon has his own unique 10 charms I'm going to kill myself as an ST.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891416#post891416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, thanks, I'll pass. Part of the risk of seeking the Exigence is the diminishment that comes with it; a god's blessing randomly mutating into an Exaltation both carries none of that risk <i>and</i> manages to cheapen Exaltation far more than Exigence itself.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why is this even a thing if the Incarnae don't suffer diminishment from their exalts? Why would a god even do this? So, a human can help save his field? If he dies, the field dies with him (albeit over time). At least with a god-blooded going SS (maybe even burning up or fusing with his parent in the process) he could take on the responsibilities of the parent in Yu-shan. I don't know, I was just spit-balling mostly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TheCountAlucard</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891416#post891416\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Hey, remember when Goku went Super Saiyan as the culmination of an entire saga's buildup, where Freeza killed off an entire planet over the <i>possibility</i> of it, where Vegeta spoke of legends in which it happened only every thousand years, and its occurrence left King Kai in awe? Then do you remember where Trunks, Vegeta, and Gohan all achieved it without <i>any</i> of that buildup? Shit, <i>Trunks' introduction to the series</i> had him going Super Saiyan, as if to show the viewers how dumb they were for buying into the hype.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>What's your point? That was one narrative. But, to repeat the narrative over and over for each character would be a waste of time. Still, both Gohan and Vegeta had emotional, life altering moments in the show that got them to SS. Trunks hinted at his. Everyone would turn into Krillin if you didn't push for more super saiyans. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T18:22:41-07:00","id":891492,"title":"","content":"I think bringing up DBZ isn't very useful since the power creep went way beyond what even PC get in games.<br /> By the end of the show Krillin was literally millions of times stronger than any other pure human before him","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11671-dramaflo","name":"DraMaFlo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11671_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"99"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T18:53:45-07:00","id":891503,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891406#post891406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I've already stated a yes to this.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sorry, must've missed that.<br /> <br /> Anyway, I'm pretty sure you can just mentally block the E-word out while reading the books. It's nothing more than nomenclature.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891418#post891418\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Good point.<br /> <br /> All in all I suspect there will be sufficient differentiation between exigent and god blooded once we have rules for both that it will be obvious that they fill very different thematic niches.<br /> <br /> *Looks at writers* <i>Right guys? </i></div> </div> </div> </div>They could hardly fail to make them fill very different niches. Even if Exigents used the same rules as the strongest godbloods, the backstories would barely overlap.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891475#post891475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is this even a thing if the Incarnae don't suffer diminishment from their exalts? Why would a god even do this? So, a human can help save his field? If he dies, the field dies with him (albeit over time).</div> </div> </div> </div>He was doomed anyway. His field's erasure would've done him in. Not sure it would've worked the other way.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> \u201cI am a god, Janest, but I am small among the<br /> ranks of immortals. When I call upon the divine flame,<br /> its price will be my consumption.\u201d The night-sounds of<br /> the spirit field faded away\u2014the crickets, the sigh of the<br /> wind\u2014and it became very quiet. \u201cThere\u2019s no other way.<br /> Come the dawn, the Fair Folk will erase this place if not<br /> stopped. This is my final day either way.\u201d </div> </div> </div>Anyway, I wouldn't be so sure about the Incarnae being undiminished.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/797631-why-craft-sucks-how-i-fixed-it\" target=\"_blank\">EX3 Craft Rewrite</a><br /> <br /> Sanctaphrax is not a person<br /> -Chejop Kejak","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1154-sanctaphrax","name":"Sanctaphrax","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1154_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1460"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T18:55:22-07:00","id":891504,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891475#post891475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Ah, the old Holden 3rd edition special. It was TEDIOUS to read through everyone's individual charms in the Antagonist section. If every demon has his own unique 10 charms I'm going to kill myself as an ST.</div> </div> </div> </div>The opposite for me. The unique Charms makes each antagonist a thousand times more exciting, especially compared to boring lists of generic Spirit Charms <span style=\"font-size:9px\">(often without even specifying the restrictions and specifics of the Charm for that particular spirit) </span><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891475#post891475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is this even a thing if the Incarnae don't suffer diminishment from their exalts?</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably did. Apparently even the Yozi were afraid of the Law of Diminishment, so I doubt creating their Exalted was without a great cost for the Incarnae - They are just mighty enough spirits to still be the most powerful people in Heaven even after that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>You need a picture altered to fit your Exalted character, or just looking for some visual inspiration? Check out the twice-reborn <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/266-photoshop-exaltification\" target=\"_blank\"> Exaltification thread</a>. And here is my <a href=\"http://danelsan.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">Deviantart page</a><br /> <br /> S\u00f8ren Kierkegaard + Kim Kardashian = <a href=\"https://twitter.com/KimKierkegaard\" target=\"_blank\">Brilliance</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/868-danelsan","name":"danelsan","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar868_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1492"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T19:01:19-07:00","id":891505,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why is this even a thing if the Incarnae don't suffer diminishment from their exalts?</div> </div> </div> </div>They did. Upon creation of the Solar Exalted the Unconquered Sun set for the first time and did so every day after that forever. His presence in Creation was greatly diminished but it was a necessary price to pay in order to create the Solars who were necessary to overthrow the Titans. I imagine the other Incarna had similar diminishments.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T19:48:33-07:00","id":891530,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891406#post891406\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Meh.</div> </div> </div> </div>I am honestly perplexed by your response to Sanctaphrax's reply. The godblooded and Exalted by way of the Exigence are as similar as the godblooded and the Exalted of the Celestial Incarna.<br /> <br /> Upon first hearing of the Exigence, while thinking it was a cool idea, I was concerned that the concept would cheapen Exaltation. When the devs stated that there were 200 to 300 tops in Creation I felt much better about it. Because there are Exalted created this way, more character types can be developed and different stories can be told that can't be told with the Exalted of the Celestial Incarna or the Dragonblooded.<br /> <br /> I am unsure of how I feel about Exigence Exalted not being targeted by the Wyld Hunt. Otoh, I can see how being able to play a celestial power level exalt openly on the Blessed Isle or areas of the Threshold where the Realm has great influence could create opportunities for stories anathema classified Exalted would not be able. At least openly.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T19:57:04-07:00","id":891534,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Holden</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891271#post891271\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The player community is naturally going to trend toward discussing &quot;Exigents&quot; as a category but that's not really how they work in the setting or how they're thought of. Outside of a few very technical First Age treatises, you won't really see anyone considering unique Exalts as belonging to a big group-category of &quot;Exigents.&quot; Just about everyone in Creation-- including elder Lunars and Sidereals-- would look at Strawmaiden Janest as &quot;the Harvest Exalt&quot; &quot;the Chosen of Ten Sheaves&quot; rather than &quot;an Exigent of a field god.&quot; The latter implies a commonality with, say, Thousand Venoms Mistress, which, holy damn, no, those two have less in common than a Solar and a Lunar do.</div> </div> </div> </div>So fun bit that came to my mind as I think on things and read this thread.<br /> <br /> &quot;Exigent&quot; is in a way like &quot;protozoan&quot;.<br /> <br /> With us eukaryotes, there historically was a division between animals, fungi, plants and single-celled stuff. Which seems simple enough at first.<br /> <br /> Except it turns out we're more related to a redwood tree than a lot of single celled things living in a pond might be related to one-another.<br /> <br /> Exigents are like those protozoans. They share a common gross feature (origin from Exigence, single-cellularity), and also share something with all other critters of their type (being Exalted, having a cell nucleus and mitochondria). But when you get into the details, being multicellular maans you are indeed more like a toadstool than amebas are like diotomes.<br /> <br /> And stuff.<br /> <br /> EDIT: God-Blooded probably are prokeryotes in this situation. &lt;_&lt;","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>And stuff.<br /> <sub><a href=\"https://blaqueandstuff.deviantart.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My DeviantArt Page</a> // <a href=\"http://blaqueandstuff.tumblr.com/\" target=\"_blank\">My tumblr</a> // <a href=\"http://www.dropbox.com/sh/trxegr5hl27s1l5/AAAegBBzxbDhvk1YpYJqdhz8a?dl=0\" target=\"_blank\">Exalted 3e Houserules</a></sub>","edited":{"userid":353,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","user":"Blaque","date":". 05-15-2016, 11:04 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":8}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/353-blaque","name":"Blaque","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar353_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T20:10:38-07:00","id":891543,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891468#post891468\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Anyways, that's not what I was saying. I was saying that it is pretty lame that the celestials and terrestrials were made by &quot;insert magic here&quot; and the exigents are created through the exigence. At least with Autochthon we had an answer (one of the creators of reality did it). This doesn't feel in theme for any of the Incarnae and the Exigence doesn't feel in theme for the Sun at all.</div> </div> </div> </div>Tyzerg, when I see people saying what you just did, I not only wish they would roll back to 'Autochton just kind of told the Incarna how to do it', but upgraded it to 'Autochton didn't do anything at all about Exaltation.'<br /> <br /> The Incarna did it. Autochton, at best, helped. He is not the one who created the Exalted, their patrons are.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-15T20:48:06-07:00","id":891554,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891543#post891543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tyzerg, when I see people saying what you just did, I not only wish they would roll back to 'Autochton just kind of told the Incarna how to do it', but upgraded it to 'Autochton didn't do anything at all about Exaltation.'<br /> <br /> The Incarna did it. Autochton, at best, helped. He is not the one who created the Exalted, their patrons are.</div> </div> </div> </div>In which edition?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3230-tyzerg","name":"Tyzerg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3230_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"131"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T00:38:24-07:00","id":891611,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Colapso</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891543#post891543\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Tyzerg, when I see people saying what you just did, I not only wish they would roll back to 'Autochton just kind of told the Incarna how to do it', but upgraded it to 'Autochton didn't do anything at all about Exaltation.'<br /> <br /> The Incarna did it. Autochton, at best, helped. He is not the one who created the Exalted, their patrons are.</div> </div> </div> </div>Eh... I think that the idea that a trickster primordial betrayed his brothers to teach the Gods the secrets of power seems suitably mythic. Though it probably ought to be portrayed that way.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>STing Bronze Age Exalted","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2402-the-wizard-of-oz","name":"The Wizard of Oz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2402_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10350"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T01:38:14-07:00","id":891620,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891554#post891554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In which edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>Until the very end of First Edition, it was not a given that Autochthon was involved in the creation of the Exalted at all. He forged the gods and taught them many things, such as the creation of tools, but there were only hints that <i>maybe </i>he taught them the secrets of Exaltation.<br /> <br /> If you go by the much beloved Games of Divinity, he merely taught the gods how to make powerful weapons and taught the Exalted how to evoke, er, harness the many secret powers of the magical materials.<br /> <br /> Incidentally, I strongly suspect that the intro of Games of Divinity was one of the primary inspirations for Exigents, especially how all the gods, from the greatest to the least, empowered champions. A fascinating detail that is never seen again, as the Incarnae and Elemental Dragons are given all the credit.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10881-anasurimbor","name":"Anasurimbor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T01:44:26-07:00","id":891622,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Anasurimbor</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891620#post891620\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Until the very end of First Edition, it was not a given that Autochthon was involved in the creation of the Exalted at all. He forged the gods and taught them many things, such as the creation of tools, but there were only hints that <i>maybe </i>he taught them the secrets of Exaltation.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they go with this direction again, there's also a simple explanation for the Castes of the Alchies and their 'resonance' with the Exalts.<br /> <br /> Autochthon didn't design his Alchemicals as the prototypes of the Classical Exalts. He designed them in <i>emulation</i> of the Exalts. The Orichalcum Castes weren't the base for the Solar Exalts, they were built to mimic the bright dazzling greatness of the Solars.<br /> <br /> (Or that's how it'll work at my table if it comes up in 21XX when the Alchie book comes out)<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Darkon</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891505#post891505\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I imagine the other Incarna had similar diminishments.</div> </div> </div> </div>Er... The Moon didn't have phases until after her Champions were made? IDK, all we've got is the mention of &quot;The First Setting of the Sun&quot; teased in that Infernal Backer Preview.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Disclaimer: In favor of fun and enjoyment, but may speak up to warn you that you're gonna step on a metaphorical land mine","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2142-kyman201","name":"Kyman201","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2142_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4086"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T01:47:12-07:00","id":891623,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891475#post891475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> So, a human can help save his field? If he dies, the field dies with him (albeit over time). At least with a god-blooded going SS (maybe even burning up or fusing with his parent in the process) he could take on the responsibilities of the parent in Yu-shan. I don't know, I was just spit-balling mostly.</div> </div> </div> </div>That wasn't even a thing in 2nd edition. If a god dies then their domain just lacks a god. If the harvest god of an area dies it doesn't mean the field dies unless the situation is such that the god was the only one keeping the field maintained. If the harvest god offs itself creating an exigent it doesn't kill the field it just leaves it unattended until a new god fills the position. As for why do it, well humans are weird creatures and not as bound as the god is by its power. Basically an exigent has more variability with it's patrons powers than the patron did. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3400-nalak42","name":"nalak42","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3400_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2931"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T02:47:51-07:00","id":891638,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891475#post891475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a god even do this?</div> </div> </div> </div> Webster's dictionary defines &quot;\u200bSelf-sacrifice&quot; as: to those who understand, no explanation is needed, and for those who do not, no explanation is possible.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T03:00:35-07:00","id":891640,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891554#post891554\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In which edition?</div> </div> </div> </div>First and Second.<br /> <br /> It was like this throughout all of First Edition, until the very last book, Exalted: the Autochtonians. But that was a book so bent on fellating its protagonists that it had wonderful things like Autochtonia defeating the Realm Navy, five Alchemicals defeating nine Deathknights on a straight-up fight (nine who served the First and Forsaken Lion, the most militaristic of Deathlords, if you are wondering if they could all fight), and the Autochtonians mocking the Perfect's scepter and then breaking it, one of the most powerful artifacts in the setting, because clearly all Autochtonian trinkets are so superior they care not for it. Oh, also, lightsabers are somehow much, much stronger than weapons of the gods forged by divine champions from the materials sacred to the most divine deities.<br /> <br /> You can see why anything printed on it is not worth of much consideration.<br /> <br /> Second edition had some passages that were also as you believe it to be... but also that were as it was in First Edition (Second Edition was very good on consistency, you see), and in fact,it was Second Edition that introduced the clause that Autochton got, in-setting, too much credit, and that was because credit that would go to other characters went to him due to bias. So it was, in fact, other Primordials, or the Incarna, the responsible for creating [Thing]. In fact, going by Second Edition canon, due to this clause, it is eminently possible that Autochton never created anything other than the Alchemical Exalted. And that only because we have the fact that he regularly keeps doing it to prove it.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>The Wizard of Oz</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891611#post891611\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Eh... I think that the idea that a trickster primordial betrayed his brothers to teach the Gods the secrets of power seems suitably mythic. Though it probably ought to be portrayed that way.</div> </div> </div> </div>Oh, I agree. Note that the post you quoted says that I ONLY think that when I see people like Tyzerg or Nephilial who believe that all the credit goes to Autochton. If giving him even a bit of credit makes people assume he has all of it, then it might be a bad idea to give him any credit at all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2617,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","user":"Colapso","date":". 05-16-2016, 06:17 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2617-colapso","name":"Colapso","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2617_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"370"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T03:13:10-07:00","id":891646,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Isator Levi</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891638#post891638\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Webster's dictionary defines &quot;\u200bSelf-sacrifice&quot; as: to those who understand, no explanation is needed, and for those who do not, no explanation is possible.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sadly, <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/self-sacrifice\" target=\"_blank\">Merriam-Webster.com just defines it as &quot;the act of giving up something that you want to have or keep in order to help someone else&quot;</a>.<br /> <br /> Either way...<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891475#post891475\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would a god even do this? So, a human can help save his field? If he dies, the field dies with him (albeit over time). At least with a god-blooded going SS (maybe even burning up or fusing with his parent in the process) he could take on the responsibilities of the parent in Yu-shan. I don't know, I was just spit-balling mostly.</div> </div> </div> </div>The death of a field god does not kill the field, neither in the short nor the long run. Gods can help, but things work fine without them. And a field god (as well as most terrestrial gods) has no duties <i>in</i> Yu-Shan whatsoever - the God who exalted Strawmaiden Janest only knew Yu-Shan from afar. (&quot;I have never walked its streets, and now I never will; perhaps you might, one day. For now, we can stand here, and look upon its lights.&quot;)<br /> They have duties <i>to</i> Yu-Shan (writing regular reports about what's going on), but that's it pretty much all they're required to do.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Silencing Whisper, <i>Eclipse</i>; Amethyst, <i>Changing Moon</i>;<br /> Daughter of Charcoal and Ash, <i>Dusk</i>, and her <i>Full Moon </i>sister;<br /> Broken Crystal, <i>Infernal </i>(<i>Night</i>-, or maybe <i>Twilight</i>-equivalent).","edited":{"userid":7262,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","user":"Amakawa Yuuto","date":". 05-16-2016, 06:15 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7262-amakawa-yuuto","name":"Amakawa Yuuto","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7262_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Aug 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"407"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T03:56:27-07:00","id":891657,"title":"","content":"Thinking about it, now we have evocations (and know that alchemicals don't really use them) it wouldn't be so bad to have beamklaives be <i>mechanically</i> superior to a regular daiklaive to make up for the fact that they don't get any cool magic powers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T04:09:11-07:00","id":891660,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Amakawa Yuuto</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891646#post891646\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sadly, <a href=\"http://www.merriam-webster.com/dictionary/self-sacrifice\" target=\"_blank\">Merriam-Webster.com just defines it as &quot;the act of giving up something that you want to have or keep in order to help someone else&quot;</a>.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hey, did I give you permission to take over for me as Forum Nitpicker? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/tongue.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Stick Out Tongue\" smilieid=\"5\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T07:06:07-07:00","id":891709,"title":"","content":"Primordi-whats? Oh whoops sorry I'm late by about 3 pages.<br /> <br /> For my money, Exigents are great because they throw a huge wrench in the gears of trying to play a role-playing game (which measures time in precise units like &quot;scenes&quot;, very technical) as a series of builds vs another series of builds because it's impossible to quantify the powers of every possible Exigent antagonist. Anything in the game which does that has my support. More support for non-quantifiable and unique elements of Creation please.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:08:08-07:00","id":891739,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ParanoiaCombo</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891709#post891709\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Primordi-whats?</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a variety of ancient Chinese fruitcake used as a foundational building material in lieu of quarriable rocks. It was reported by the French Durand expedition of 1971 that the Great Wall of China was actually around 50% Primordial by volume, but this report was later found to be in error.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writer for Exalted.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2093-crumplepunch","name":"Crumplepunch","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2093_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1976"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:22:01-07:00","id":891748,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tyzerg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891414#post891414\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Probably not, although that would be cool for Gods who can't do the whole exigence thing or for whatever reason...</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really responding to Tyzerg specifically, but this post does neatly encapsulate something which has been bothering me, both in this thread and in the larger discussion of Exigents.<br /> <br /> Can't make an Exigent &quot;for whatever reason&quot;? For example, such a reason <i>might</i> entail NOT being one of a tiny handful of beings in Creation at any given time to whom the Sun grants such awesome autonomy? As in, the same long odds as becoming a Solar? It both confuses and infuriates me* how people will just casually talk about gods getting Exigents at-will (like the plan to make gods, so those gods could then go make custom Exigents for you), but nobody seems to say &quot;hey, any mortal could bring down the Perfect: first, they become a Solar, and then...&quot; - why the disconnect?<br /> <br /> And, sure, there's fewer gods than mortals in Creation (discounting Least Gods, and <i>please let's all agree to do that</i>), but there's also less Exigency than Solaritude in Creation, once the prison shatters:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>John M\u00f8rke</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">There were low numbers of Exigents in the early and middle of the First Age. By the end they had dropped off drastically, as no new ones were being made. There are likely less than 100 Exigents around when the Empress vanishes, maybe even significantly fewer than 50 across all of Creation. The number is expected to rise with the return of the Solars, but not drastically. Gods who are corrupt, indolent, and wicked are going to need to fish Exigency off the &quot;black market.&quot;</div> </div> </div> </div>In other words, when people say &quot;any god can make an Exigent,&quot; that doesn't really mean you should assume a large portion of them <i>do</i>.<br /> <br /> <br /> * Okay, no, I'm not angry. Just rewatching a bunch of Futurama.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;For me, there's no fundamental conflict between really loving something and also seeing it as very profoundly flawed.&quot; -- Jay Eddidin","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2168-chejop-kejak","name":"Chejop Kejak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2168_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1219"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T08:24:27-07:00","id":891750,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Kyman201</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891622#post891622\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Er... The Moon didn't have phases until after her Champions were made? IDK, all we've got is the mention of 'The First Setting of the Sun' teased in that Infernal Backer Preview.</div> </div> </div> </div>No. All the Moon's phases were on display all the time! Kinda like how Luna could be in multiple places at the same time in 2E, multiple Moons displaying each phase were always in the sky! After the Law of Diminishment took effect on Luna, she only had one Moon in the sky for part of a day displaying one phase at a time. At least that what it says in my head after making it up! :P<br /> <br /> Unless I am mistaken all the Incarnae suffered the Law of Diminishment in some fashion after making their Chosen. It may not have been as obvious as the UcS. IMO all gods should experience the Law of Dimishment for creating Exalted. IIRC they do, but the price is not always obvious to others nor is it always the same.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Good night sweet Green Sun Prince: And flights of demons beat thee to thy rest...with billyclubs! <img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://theonyxpath.com/forum/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/362-darkon","name":"Darkon","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar362_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"228"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-16T09:26:31-07:00","id":891803,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891748#post891748\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> And, sure, there's fewer gods than mortals in Creation (discounting Least Gods, and <i>please let's all agree to do that</i>),</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't know... even without the concept of least gods, I could see a case for humans being outnumbered by gods (even if most gods are not very significant).<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Chejop Kejak</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">In other words, when people say &quot;any god can make an Exigent,&quot; that doesn't really mean you should assume a large portion of them <i>do</i>.<br /></div> </div> </div> </div>It makes me think of a similar disconnect I have with Nobilis, regarding the subject of how many Estates there are against the implications that there are only ever around a thousand Nobles.<br /> <br /> In either case, it helps t remember that the core premise is an invitation for diversity, not multiplicity.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T01:55:47-07:00","id":892385,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891412#post891412\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Do we even still need endowment-created god blooded any more?</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm fine with spirits empowering people but I don't like their default name being god blooded because words mean things.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T05:16:57-07:00","id":892430,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=892385#post892385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with spirits empowering people but I don't like their default name being god blooded because words mean things.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe if there's a special transfusion involved...? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>He/him","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/177-thecountalucard","name":"TheCountAlucard","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar177_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10857"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T06:05:42-07:00","id":892446,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lioness</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=892385#post892385\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm fine with spirits empowering people but I don't like their default name being god blooded because words mean things.</div> </div> </div> </div> If I could find a distinct clip of Jorah Mormont falling to his knees and calling Daenarys blood of my blood, I would be happier.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T06:37:35-07:00","id":892455,"title":"","content":"Part of my problem is that god blooded was basically appropriated as a power catagory in 2e (arguably the fanon already did this in 1e) and weaker children of spirits were effectively pushed out of it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b><a href=\"https://swordofcreation.net/\" target=\"_blank\">Sword of Creation</a> a hub for Exalted related content</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/7-lioness","name":"Lioness","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar7_2.png","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5443"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T07:33:34-07:00","id":892490,"title":"","content":"\u200b<a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/84-holden\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar84_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"84\" data-vbnamecard=\"84\">Holden</a> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/86-john-m\u00f8rke\" style=\"background-image:url('https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5//avatar86_2.png');\" class=\"b-bbcode-user b-bbcode-user--has-avatar js-bbcode-user\" data-userid=\"86\" data-vbnamecard=\"86\">John M\u00f8rke</a> , thanks for the succinct and insightful clarifications on the thread!<br /> <br /> Here's the way I think of Exigents. First, there's fewer than a hundred of them at any one time (fewer even than the Sidereals), and a decent chunk of those are one-off, never returning if they die. Second, each one is unique, not rare, but absolutely one-of-a-kind. Third, nobody in Exalted as the benefits of a game book, or a DBZ scouter to give them omniscient info.<br /> <br /> When I roll that up into the setting, I get several dozen people with unique and strange powers running around doing their thing. That is not a recipe for overwhelming/overshadowing the existing Exalts. It is a recipe for interesting and different allies/antagonists to the existing Exalts, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6601-totentanz","name":"Totentanz","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6601_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T07:34:03-07:00","id":892493,"title":"","content":"Wrong thread. &gt;: (","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"color:#00ffff\">I have approximate knowledge of many things.</span><br /> <a href=\"https://forum.rpg.net/index.php?threads/wip-xenoblade-chronicles-the-sword-can-see-the-future.835575/\" target=\"_blank\">Write up as I play Xenoblade Chronicles.</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/158-isator-levi","name":"Isator Levi","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar158_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"17901"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2016-05-17T15:23:11-07:00","id":892821,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Crumplepunch</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/exalted/exigents/890803-the-exigence?p=891739#post891739\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's a variety of ancient Chinese fruitcake used as a foundational building material in lieu of quarriable rocks. It was reported by the French Durand expedition of 1971 that the Great Wall of China was actually around 50% Primordial by volume, but this report was later found to be in error.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is the best post about Primordials ever written on any board about Exalted ever. This is the new standard. Let's keep it that way <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/smile.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Smile\" smilieid=\"1\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Incentive is not permission or justification.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/255-paranoiacombo","name":"ParanoiaCombo","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar255_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"526"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}